# Concrete node types each cluster's sweeps can ever look at, collected once per module so the
# loops never re-test a type they cannot use. Every entry is traceable to a predicate that reads
# the loop variable itself:
#   cluster2: 12685/12694 Import+ImportFrom, 12872 FunctionDef, 12879 Compare, 12889 With,
#             12900/13051/13063/13067 Assign+AnnAssign+Return, 12901/13097/13112 Assign/AugAssign,
#             12923/13075/13131 Call.
#   cluster3: 13382/13391 Import+ImportFrom, 13581/13617/14128 Assign, 13589 FunctionDef +
#             AsyncFunctionDef, 13637/14132 Dict, 13647/13658/13668 Attribute+Name, and
#             Call-only from 13679/13689/14116 onwards (the 20-rule finale sits behind that).
#   cluster1: the emit loop hands every node to `_c1_cluster1_candidates`, whose whole body is one
#             isinstance chain over the loop variable -- 12595 Call, 12668 Subscript, 12674 Dict,
#             12681 Assign+AnnAssign, 12692 FunctionDef (lines as of this edit). A node of any other
#             type reaches no branch, returns an empty list, and the emit loop's only statement is
#             `for cwe_meta in that-list`, so such a row cannot produce a sink, a dedupe key or a
#             sink id. The two table sweeps that read this same list want a subset of it:
#             `_c1_namespace_history` (12498) tests Assign/AnnAssign and
#             `_c1_template_string_consumers` (12544) tests Call, both already in the set, so
#             filtering once changes neither table.
# AsyncFunctionDef and AsyncWith are listed even where only FunctionDef/With is tested: the two
# are siblings on some Python versions and subclasses on others, and a node kept by mistake can
# never lose a finding, while a node dropped by mistake can. AnnAssign/AugAssign are carried in
# the cluster 3 set for the same reason.
_GATE_CLUSTER1 = frozenset({
    ast.Call, ast.Subscript, ast.Dict, ast.Assign, ast.AnnAssign,
    ast.FunctionDef, ast.AsyncFunctionDef,
})
_GATE_CLUSTER2 = frozenset({
    ast.Import, ast.ImportFrom, ast.FunctionDef, ast.AsyncFunctionDef, ast.Compare,
    ast.With, ast.AsyncWith, ast.Assign, ast.AnnAssign, ast.AugAssign, ast.Return, ast.Call,
})
_GATE_CLUSTER3 = frozenset({
    ast.Import, ast.ImportFrom, ast.Assign, ast.AnnAssign, ast.AugAssign,
    ast.FunctionDef, ast.AsyncFunctionDef, ast.Dict, ast.Attribute, ast.Name, ast.Call,
})
# Two more sweeps that walk a whole module list and then reject almost every row on its own first
# line. Each set is the union of the loop's own head tests, so a row removed here is a row the rules
# were already rejecting - and the engine defines no `ast` node subclasses (no `class X(ast.Call)`
# or similar anywhere in this file), so exact-type membership and the callee's `isinstance` answer the
# same question for every tree `ast.parse` can produce.
#   _GATE_CWE93: `_collect_cwe93_header_injection`'s first loop. `exprs` is filled only under
#                `isinstance(node, ast.Assign)` and `isinstance(node, ast.Call)`, and the body's next
#                statement is `if not exprs: continue`. Attribute, Constant and Subscript appear in
#                this rule only as tests on `node.targets`, `node.func` and `node.slice` - never as
#                the loop node - so they are deliberately NOT in the set. The second loop in the same
#                pass already opens with its own `isinstance(node, ast.Assign)` test and is unchanged.
#   _GATE_BATCH3B: `_collect_batch3b_structural_findings`' rule dispatch loop, whose entire body is
#                `cwe_meta = None`, one `if/elif` chain on Call / (Assign, AnnAssign) /
#                (Return with a value), and `if cwe_meta:`. Nothing else in the loop runs per node,
#                so a row outside the set leaves `cwe_meta` None and hands out no sink id.
#                The three flag pre-scans above it (imports, try/finally, whitelist) keep their own
#                single type tests and are untouched.
#   _GATE_CWE319_VARS: `_collect_cwe319_variable_resolution_findings`' only module-node loop. Its
#                head test is `if not isinstance(func, (ast.FunctionDef, ast.AsyncFunctionDef)):
#                continue` and the body opens on `func.args`, so a definition is the whole
#                population the loop can use. Subtree walks inside the body (`ast.walk(func)`) are
#                not module sweeps and are deliberately not touched.
_GATE_CWE93 = frozenset({ast.Assign, ast.Call})
_GATE_BATCH3B = frozenset({ast.Call, ast.Assign, ast.AnnAssign, ast.Return})
_GATE_CWE319_VARS = frozenset({ast.FunctionDef, ast.AsyncFunctionDef})

